  "body": {
    "id": "lem:component-aligned-live-fragment-right-congruence",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Fix \\((P,B^0,\\varepsilon,\\Gamma,\\pi_0)\\in\\mathfrak M_{p,m}^{\\mathrm{CA}}\\) and its observed moments \\(\\mathcal O_G\\), and let \\(\\rho,\\rho'\\) be prefixes in \\(\\mathcal D_G^{\\mathrm{live}}\\) ending at the same removed set \\(A\\).  Then \\(F(\\rho)=F(\\rho')\\) if and only if \\(\\operatorname{Comp}_{\\mathrm{CA}}(\\rho)=\\operatorname{Comp}_{\\mathrm{CA}}(\\rho')\\).  Unequal fragments have disjoint nonempty completion sets, and the legal suffix paths depend only on \\(A\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P",
      "B0",
      "epsilon",
      "Gamma",
      "pi0",
      "M_CA",
      "p",
      "m",
      "O_G",
      "G",
      "rho",
      "D_live",
      "A",
      "F_rho",
      "Comp_rho"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:component-aligned-limvam-class",
      "def:live-fragment-completions",
      "def:removed-set-compatibility-dag",
      "lem:original-row-invariance"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "A legal suffix is a path from \\(A\\) to \\(V\\) in the fixed DAG \\(\\mathcal D_G^{\\mathrm{live}}\\), so legality depends only on \\(A\\), not on the prefix.  Source-to-sink pruning makes at least one such suffix available.  If a suffix removes \\(r_1,\\ldots,r_{p-|A|}\\), then \\(\\texttt{lem:original-row-invariance}\\) shows that it appends exactly the rows in (7), independently of the prefix.  Equal fragments therefore have equal completion sets.  If a tuple lies in the intersection of two completion sets, its projection onto the already assigned rows \\(A\\) equals each prefix fragment, so the fragments are equal.  Nonemptiness turns equality of completion sets into a nonempty intersection, proving the reverse implication; contraposition gives disjointness.",
    "justification": "Source-to-sink pruning supplies nonempty completions, and immutable rows make the fragment relation a right congruence on the q-DAG.",
    "gap": "Dead prefixes make the converse false because unequal fragments can both have empty completion sets.",
    "consumer": "The pairing-informative enumerator can merge live prefixes safely.",
